atlas external

architecture foreign-twin
  canonical_name ForeignTwinGraph
  family external
  domain External
  layer external
  semantic_question What is the current cached projection of an externally-owned resource, and what rights do we hold over it?
  purpose Remote stays remote. A content-addressed cached projection with rights observe/reference/bind/act. Materialize ingests the projection into the fabric.
  maturity measured
  node_types ForeignTwin
  node_types Projection
  edge_types projects
  edge_types materializes_to
  state_types observe
  state_types reference
  state_types bind
  state_types act
  invariant a retained body is found under the foreign root this estate is told to use, by the name its receipt gave it, and never outside that directory: a receipt records where a reading happened, not where the estate keeps its evidence now, and an estate that can only read its own bodies from the absolute path they were first written to cannot be moved, restored, or carried onto another machine
  invariant every native Project foreign verb derives missing receipt and body directories from BONFYRE_FOREIGN_ROOT; explicit leaf-directory settings retain precedence and an overlong derived path refuses without falling back to another store
  invariant a cached projection is not remote truth
  invariant a retained observation body is parsed only while it still hashes to its receipt
  invariant a retained observation body path is immutable after receipt materialization
  invariant a refetch whose bytes match the prior receipt's content_sha256 leaves the retained file in place; a changed body of 64 KiB or more is settled on APFS with transparent compression at the same path, so readers and receipt digests see identical bytes (settle_retained_body in components/BonfyreProject/src/main.c, witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/retained_body_settle_test.sh)
  forbidden_inference a compressed retained body -> different evidence; the compression is filesystem allocation, and every read returns the bytes the receipt hashed
  invariant a private institutional or self ForeignTwin observation retains its body and receipt below its closure-derived estate/scope or actor root; the public foreign carrier and a sibling institutional or actor closure cannot enumerate it
  invariant a self ForeignTwin workspace enumerates and inspects only receipt filenames derived below the current authenticated actor root, rehashes a selected retained body against its receipt before showing an excerpt, and never accepts a body path, actor root, or public ForeignTwin coordinate from the browser
  invariant a projected candidate carries the receipt digest of the body it was read from
  invariant a retained-body exact query answers only whether ForeignTwin currently has a receipt for that exact subject and predicate; it remains separate from body rehash, semantic relevance, and every admission decision
  invariant a housing AvailabilityCandidate requires a current public observe right, allow decision, attempted fetch, and successful robots preflight on its ForeignTwin receipt
  invariant a source excluded by robots or an absent observe right is receipted without fetching its source URL
  invariant a bounded byte-range observation preflights robots and observe right before fetching, caps the received body, records sample_observed rather than a full source observation, and never promotes partial bytes as a complete foreign identity
  invariant a bounded full-response observation caps the received body without requesting a byte range, refuses redirects because a robots check cannot silently move to another host, and emits source_observed only for a complete successful response; transient design-anatomy bytes may be released after receipt-bound measurement without claiming current availability
  invariant the product release projection joins published source contracts to SourceFrontier's authored exact_address (using legacy address only when the ledger has no exact_address column), then joins ItemArchive and observed-price reductions by exact authored source coordinate through bounded indexes; it carries separately authored spatial, media, rights and publisher extraction declarations, and reads distinct SiteProgram identities only through its authored source_collection source_refs bridge: collection fanout is not multiple programs, and program input is never a rendered route or verified delivery
  invariant a cross-domain readiness path is only an independently-owned input closure for a later compiler: a declared extractor plus retained archive material is ready_for_extraction and not an extracted spatial/media/rights fact; publisher remains a declared identifier; economics reaches observed only through exact authored source-coordinate price binding; each missing path names its blocked binding
  invariant a ForeignTwin page is a bounded carrier slice while release_summary is calculated over the entire owner closure; offset/limit affects only which rich rows cross the carrier, never the reported estate census, readiness totals, economics totals or public-program input totals
  invariant a ForeignTwin query is a bounded case-insensitive literal filter over authored source-contract fields (URL, source identity, family, carries, or declared publisher); it returns result total and estate_total separately, never claims semantic relevance, ownership, classification, or a changed whole-estate readiness frontier
  invariant every bounded source-release page is deterministically ordered and carries a locally-derived catalogue_generation over its exact owner projection; a later page that names a different expected generation is refused as snapshot_mismatch rather than silently combining two working-set releases. This generation states only local projection continuity, never remote-world immutability or the cause of a change
  invariant price observations join a ForeignTwin only through an exact authored source coordinate; an unmatched economic source identity stays visible as unbound rather than being guessed from publisher wording, hostname similarity, item title, or family
  cannot_infer source admission or archive depth -> public program, distribution route, reuse licence, external authority, price quote, or purchase authority
  forbidden_inference foreign twin cache -> remote authority
  forbidden_inference observe right -> bind or act right
  forbidden_inference retained body -> verified availability
  forbidden_inference weak public supply signal -> exact availability fact
  forbidden_inference policy exclusion -> absence of external inventory
  computational_form durable
  native_format graf
  command BonfyreProject
