  internal_calculus a receipt carries two independent sets of facts about one representation: this estate's digest of the bytes it retained, and the source's own statements about what it served -- ETag, Last-Modified, Content-Type, Content-Location, Link rel=license and rel=canonical, RFC 9530 Content-Digest and Repr-Digest, and whether an RFC 9421 message signature was present. Keeping only the first loses the only machine-readable statement of rights a source ever makes
  internal_calculus re-observation is conditional whenever a prior receipt carries a validator. Receipts append, so the newest line is the one read for it; a 304 becomes a new observation at a new knowledge time that references the prior body rather than retaining a second copy of it
  invariant a source-supplied digest is held apart from this estate's own and neither is promoted to the other; ours proves the bytes have not drifted since retention and the source's is what the publisher asserted about what it served
  invariant robots permitting a read is not a licence to republish; Link rel=license is a separate fact, it is usually absent, and absent means the source stated none rather than that permission exists
  invariant a validator is handed back to a source exactly as the source issued it; an ETag contains quotes and a parser that stops at the first one returns a mangled validator that every source ignores, which makes conditional re-observation appear to work while never having worked
  cannot_infer a 304 -> the thing not having changed in the world; it says the representation this estate holds is still current
  cannot_infer a completed sweep -> permission to republish anything it read
  cannot_infer a boundary response -> a source that does not exist; it is what the transport said at that moment
  cannot_infer policy_excluded -> a source refusing this estate specifically; robots is a standing rule the source wrote for everyone
  cannot_infer an RFC 9421 message signature verifying -> factual correctness or reuse permission; it is communication authenticity
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/http_envelope_test.sh observes a source that issues a strong validator and proves the envelope is recorded separately from this estate's digest, that the recorded ETag still contains the quotes the source issued, and that observing again returns 304 and produces a repeat_observed receipt carrying zero bytes and the prior body's digest rather than a duplicate body. It skips rather than passes when the source is unreachable, because a network witness that passes offline is testing nothing
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/foreign_release_projection_test.sh builds independent source, frontier and archive owners; proves their stages join without a receipt directory; and proves public program is still unbound rather than inferred from admission or retained material
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/foreign_release_projection_test.sh proves a price ledger reports one exact source-contract binding and one unbound incoming price source separately, without turning either into an offer or economic authority
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/foreign_release_projection_test.sh proves a normalized SourceFrontier address cannot displace the matching authored exact_address when joining a published source contract
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/foreign_release_projection_test.sh proves a published SiteProgram reaches an exact source only through a published SourceCollection source_refs declaration, and records input_bound with delivery not_verified rather than a public page
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tools/foreign-sweep.sh observed 400 occurrences of the estate against real sources at one request each with a quarter-second pace: 47 retained a body, 30 returned 304 to a conditional request and became repeat_observed, 15 answered a boundary response, 1 was excluded by robots, and 307 could not have their robots preflighted and are recorded as policy_indeterminate rather than read anyway. 39 sources issued an ETag; none stated a machine-readable licence, none signed the message, and none supplied an RFC 9530 digest
  known_gap 307 of 400 sources could not have robots preflighted, so they were not read. That is the law working and it is also the dominant outcome: most of this estate cannot currently be observed at all, and whether that is unreachable hosts, redirect chains or WAFs is not yet separated.
  known_gap the sweep is driven by hand and nothing schedules it. A plan is compiled, a bounded slice is observed, and no timer widens it; the estate moves when someone runs it.
  known_gap no source in the observed slice stated a machine-readable licence. Link rel=license was absent on every one, so every rights question in the estate still rests on a human reading terms, which is a fact about how the web publishes rights rather than about this observer.
  known_gap foreign observe now preflights a declared public observe right and robots.txt, preserving policy_excluded separately from a target boundary_response, and retains an allowed body under --body so a downstream reader can bind to exact receipted bytes. Retained Craigslist, Sublet.com property-card, and direct AppFolio public portal bodies now project only provenance-bound candidates; source-bound housing frontiers preserve direct, legacy-social, conditional-economics, feature-claim, and public-map proximity tiers rather than scoring unknown facts together. Geographic mapping retains Nominatim/Overpass source response digests and performs geodesic proximity plus park-first reverse discovery, without inferring a walk route, entrance distance, unit-specific exterior right, pet acceptance, or availability. A candidate is still not verified availability because verification would need a forbidden contact effect. The retained Sublet Dallas response currently lacks the required policy-preflight facts and visibly serves non-Dallas cards, so it remains non-promotable until a compliant Dallas observation exists. Other retained direct-source shapes remain unparsed.
  invariant an observation is never overwritten: a 404 at one time and retained bytes at another are two records, and the relation between them is computed rather than resolved by keeping only the newer
  invariant current content and current availability are separate answers; the most recent observation that retained bytes and the most recent observation of any kind are different questions, and reporting one as both hides bytes held from a source that no longer serves them
  invariant a resource that never retained content reports null reachability, not false; false would claim the content held is unreachable about content that was never held
  forbidden_inference a superseded observation -> a deleted one (it remains recorded and readable through history)
  forbidden_inference a listed conflict -> a source that lied (content changing is ordinary; the institution only has to know its earlier belief is no longer current)
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/src/main.c
  witness bonfyre-project foreign conflicts over 35 real receipts reports 3 disagreeing resources: feed.xml with 4 content changes still reachable, sitemap-notes.xml with 2, and an okta endpoint that has only ever answered 404
  invariant observation, promotion and claim are three standings and none is ownership: observing records that something answered, promoting means the institution chose to be able to name it, and claiming is an assertion by some institution
  invariant a twin is promoted only when an observation actually retained bytes; its identity digest is the content digest that was retained and its evidence_ref names the receipt that retained it, so an identity whose digest was invented cannot exist
  invariant a twin's identity derives from the address it was observed at, not from a receipt filename that changes every observation
  invariant a promoted twin carries an address and a presence, and its presence is LIVE: an observation of the real world stays real even when a demo institution is the one looking
  invariant two subjects sharing an identity digest are reported rather than merged; which id is canonical is not the storage layer's call, and collapsing them would strand whatever already references the loser
  forbidden_inference a promoted twin -> a claimed, verified or owned one
  forbidden_inference a claim -> a verified relationship (AssertionBoundary and Authority decide what it is worth)
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/foreign_twin_test.sh promotes 14 observed resources idempotently, refuses 4 that never retained content, reports 7 duplicate identities without merging them, and proves no claim points at a subject that does not exist
  invariant an observation that retains content promotes its resource in the same act; the one moment an identity is unambiguous is when the bytes that identify it are in hand, and deferring it invites an identity derived later by a different rule beside the one derived here
  invariant a failed promotion does not fail the observation; the receipt is written and the bytes are kept, so a resource that could not be named stays observable
  invariant promotion refuses a private closure: an observation under an estate or actor root belongs to whoever took it, and publishing one as a public subject would make it readable by everything that can read the Matrix. A caller that means to promote privately must say so and say into which scope
  invariant an identity is derived only from a body that still hashes to its receipt; a drifted body is no longer the thing the receipt describes, and an identity taken from it would be attested by a receipt for different content
  invariant the estate observes two shapes of external thing and they do not identify the same way: a URL twin is one resource fetched repeatedly, identified by the bytes it last returned; a source is an endpoint observed across many pages, identified by a digest over its sorted distinct page digests
  invariant a source twin carries no web address, because the estate holds no route to it; binding an invented URL would assert a route that cannot resolve, which is worse than having none. A presence is still bound, because the source is a real thing observed in the live world
  invariant a source identity moves when what the source serves moves and not otherwise; an identity that drifted on re-observation would make every source a new thing each time it was looked at
  invariant a claim derived from an observation requires the read to have been authorized under the policy recorded at the time: public observe right, allow decision, attempted fetch, and a successful robots preflight where a 404 counts as success. A body digest proves what a parser read and never that it was permitted to
  invariant the admission law is not housing-shaped; any derived claim needs the same five facts, and holding it in one domain's normalizer made it unaskable by anything else
  forbidden_inference an admissible receipt -> a true or useful claim (it says the read was authorized, and nothing about what the bytes say)
  invariant registration and activation are different acts: registering establishes that a stable foreign identity exists, and binds no presence. Observing something does not make it present in this institution's world, or a partner, provider, opportunity or offer
  invariant activation and deactivation are authority-gated in both directions; turning a subject on or off in the world is an act, not a side effect of having looked at it
  forbidden_inference a registered twin -> an active, present, or partnered one
  invariant not every twin is mirrored: a hydration regime is authored per twin from MIRROR-LIKE, INDEXED, REMOTE and EPHEMERAL, and a twin with no authored regime is reported as unpoliced rather than defaulted, because an unmade decision is not a decision to mirror
  invariant cooling removes bodies a regime says not to keep and never removes a receipt; it reduces what is held, never what is known to have been seen
  invariant a regime is enforced where the body is written, not only by a later sweep; a cleanup is undone by the next observation, so a decision not to retain survived exactly until someone looked again
  invariant a twin with no authored regime retains its body; an unmade decision must not silently start discarding evidence, so the safe direction is to keep
  invariant a twin's applicable actions derive from what it is, not from the fact that it is foreign: subject kind ForeignTwin says only that authority is elsewhere, and investigating ownership is meaningless for a specification as mapping a vocabulary is for a tax roll
  invariant a twin's kind is authored rather than inferred from its address; guessing a kind from a hostname is how a merchant becomes a dataset
  invariant a kind nobody has declared actions for affords nothing rather than falling back to a generic set; an empty aperture list is an honest answer and a borrowed one is not
  forbidden_inference a classified kind -> a verified one (someone asserted this is a property source, and that is an assertion like any other)
  invariant the columnar observation estate is a material-plane closure contribution, not a file the estate happens to query; a subject whose closure omits the bytes backing it describes an identity and not a thing
  invariant a Parquet row is not an admitted Matrix fact, a subject_candidate is not a MatrixSubject, and an observation row is not a RelationshipGraph edge; the columnar estate is a compressed factual representation and AssertionBoundary still controls admission
  invariant a columnar body that is a directory of parts is identified by a manifest digest over its sorted members; digesting one member would describe part of the body as though it were all of it
  invariant a closure resource is portable: a filesystem path is a reference only one host can follow, so contributions carry bonfyre://, https:// or urn: and never a local path
  forbidden_inference a bound body -> an admitted fact or a licence to redistribute it
  invariant a closure can be taken over any subject with an active presence, not only one a hostname resolves to; closures addressed by host alone silently limited the manifest to institutions, and an observation source has no route at all
  invariant the closure manifest carries each plane's contributions with owner, representation, resource and exact digest, in both the crate and the field carrier; a manifest that says references are listed below and lists none is worse than one that says the plane is sparse
  forbidden_inference a resolvable closure -> a reachable subject
  invariant Parquet and Zarr compose rather than compete: the columnar body holds durable observation facts and the field holds their chunked arrangement, and lowering one into the other is an ordinary derivation
  invariant a derived field carries its lineage in its own attributes -- the exact digest of the body it was lowered from, the derivation that produced it, and the observation frontier at that moment -- so a cell is traceable to the rows, sources and owners it counts
  invariant a field reconciles with the corpus it came from; a grid whose total does not match the observations it aggregates is describing something else
  forbidden_inference a derived field -> a new observation (it is one arrangement of the rows it was computed from, and it is stale the moment they change)
  forbidden_inference a field cell -> a fact about the world (a source observed twice as often is not twice as real)
  witness a 115x17 int32 field lowered from the columnar body sums to 6,535,062 -- the whole corpus -- and its dallas-tax-parcels row sums to 499,388, the same number that source's DERIVE aperture returns
  witness a crate and a zarr group over foreign_twin:src-dallas-tax-parcels each carry the Parquet body with its 64-character digest and slice selector
  witness 115 source slices of a 569,864,921-byte columnar body bound on the material plane, one manifest digest, one slice selector per source
  witness a parcel source affords Property.investigateOwnership and Property.economics while a specification affords Research.mapVocabulary on the same binary; a reference asset affords nothing
  invariant an absent body and a changed body are different facts: a body present and hashing differently is drift and refuses promotion, while a body cooled under its regime promotes on the receipt digest that still identifies it
  forbidden_inference a regime -> a licence (retaining bytes because a regime permits it does not make retention lawful)
