  forbidden_inference a large catalogue -> a large reach

architecture retained-body-service
  canonical_name RetainedBodyService
  family external
  domain External / Retained bytes
  layer surface
  semantic_question When the estate serves bytes it retained, are they the right bytes, and are they the newest?
  purpose Twice, no. A receipt is a twin's whole history, one observation per line, appended forever; the route read the first 64KB and took the last complete line inside that prefix, so any twin whose history outgrew the buffer served an observation from the middle of its past as if it were current -- hn-front-page was answering with bytes ten hours old and a stale timestamp to prove it. Worse, the field reader returned without touching its output when a key was absent, so body_path kept whatever the previous request had left in that stack slot; the inherited path passed the inside-the-bodies-directory guard because it was a real body, and the estate replied 200 with one twin's retained bytes under another twin's name and an empty digest header.
  maturity measured
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/src/main.c
  consumes ForeignTwin
  publishes DerivedView
  internal_calculus the receipt is read from its end, so the newest observation is found at the same cost whatever the history weighs. The body path comes from that line or from nowhere. A retained body is fetched beside its destination and moved into place, so a reader sees the previous observation or the new one and never half of one.
  invariant the newest observation is the one served; an estate that keeps every observation has a history that only grows, so reading from the head is a bug that arrives by waiting
  invariant a field that is absent leaves nothing behind; a reader that returns without clearing hands the next caller the last caller's answer, and the buffers here are reused across requests
  invariant bytes are served under the twin that retained them or not at all; a body with no digest is a body whose receipt did not name it, and serving it anyway is a provenance failure wearing a 200
  invariant a retained body is replaced atomically; writing into the file the estate serves means a reader during the fetch sees a truncation, and the reheat rewrites the hot twins every five minutes
  invariant a failed fetch does not replace a good observation; moving an empty file into place would delete the last real one and report success
  cannot_infer retained bytes -> a claim that they are true or current; they are what a source served at a moment
  cannot_infer a served body -> a live source; the receipt says when it was read
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/internet-census.test.mjs checks native retained-body readers clear absent fields, bind bytes to each twin's digest, read the latest complete receipt line, and atomically replace bodies after successful fetch; live estate checks are opt-in and are not implied by fixture success
  known_gap the receipt tail is read into a fixed buffer, so a single observation line longer than that buffer would still be cut; no line approaches it today and nothing checks
  known_gap the digest is served and never verified against the bytes; a body corrupted on disk would be served under a digest it no longer matches

architecture content-quarantine
  canonical_name ContentQuarantine
  family external
  domain External / Presentation state
  layer surface
  semantic_question Should this retained material be projected automatically, and who decided?
  purpose The estate reads thousands of external sources and projects what it reads onto four public front doors. Nothing stood between an ugly item in a feed, a scraped page or a social source and a full-width card on .life or .live. This is the screen, the boxed state and the exclusion -- and it is deliberately not a moderation product: the observation, its receipt and its bytes are untouched, and a flag decides presentation rather than truth.
  maturity measured
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/content_flag.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/content_screen.json
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/build/content-screens.jsonl
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/build/install_authored_rows.mjs
  witness site/matrix/surfaces/build/authored_rows.test.mjs imports four authored screen declarations into a local CMS and keeps declared-only screens distinct from installed screens without contacting a remote estate
  source_path scripts/content_screen.py.archive
  source_path scripts/content-screen.cue
  source_path scripts/content-screen.mjs
  source_path scripts/Makefile
  source_path deploy/systemd/bonfyre-content-screen.service
  source_path deploy/systemd/bonfyre-content-screen.timer
  witness scripts/tests/content_screen.test.mjs proves the Bun screen keeps a missing private term list distinct from a clean result, matches transformed spellings and edge words, uses the latest receipt, writes one redacted boxed flag through CMS, and does not disclose the term; normalization matched the retired Python peer on eight spelling cases before cutover
  witness scripts/tests/content_screen_install.test.mjs proves the Bun/CUE runtime stages under the systemd path and installed execution reports missing private terms without claiming a clean scan
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/_kit.js
  consumes ForeignTwin
  publishes DerivedView
  internal_calculus a screen is authored with what it looks at, what it can see and what it demonstrably cannot. The installed text screen normalises transformed spellings -- case, diacritics, digit and symbol substitutions, and separators inserted between letters -- and matches an authored term list against the normalised form. A match writes a flag naming the twin, the screen, the redacted term and a review state; the reader asks for the boxed set and declines to project it.
  invariant flagged is not illegal, false, malicious or deleted, and not flagged is not safe; the flag says only that this must not be projected automatically until its presentation state is resolved, and the type carries that in its own cannot_infer
  invariant the observation, its receipt and its bytes are untouched; boxing is a presentation state and a cleared flag restores ordinary projection
  invariant a screen states what it cannot see; this one matches spellings and is blind to meaning, context, quotation and reclaimed use, which is why a match is a reason to look rather than a finding
  invariant a declared screen is not a running one, and its silence is not a clean bill; a screen installed with no terms reports that it looked at nothing rather than returning an empty result
  invariant a matched term is recorded redacted; a flag is read by people on a page and must not reprint in full what it was raised for
  invariant the term list lives on the estate and not in this repository; a list of slurs is not something to commit, and a screen with no list says so
  invariant a substitution stands for a letter only between letters, and only runs of single letters are rejoined; without the first, trailing punctuation joins the word, and without the second, ordinary prose folds into false matches
  cannot_infer a flag -> a judgement about the material or its source
  cannot_infer an unflagged twin -> a screened and cleared one; most material is never looked at by a screen that could see anything
  cannot_infer a screen declared -> a screen running; obscenity and NSFWJS are recorded with their provenance and produce no flags in this estate
  witness scripts/tests/content_screen.test.mjs holds ten transformed spellings against the native matcher and four pieces of ordinary prose against false matching, checks term redaction and the missing-term refusal, checks the ordinary reader excludes boxed twins without erasing the observation, and carries opt-in live checks that every flag names its screen and every declared screen says its silence is not a result; the historical Python test is retained as components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_content_quarantine.py.archive
  known_gap only text is screened; the image screen is declared and not installed, because classifying pictures means fetching and holding them, which changes what the estate retains rather than only what it screens
  known_gap screening runs over retained bodies on demand rather than at ingest, so material is boxed after it lands rather than before it is first projectable
  known_gap the native screen has fixture-level CMS and scheduled-unit witnesses, but the timer has not been deployed or exercised on a live estate
  known_gap review has a state and no surface to change it; a boxed item stays boxed until somebody edits the record directly

