  invariant the workbench keeps observations and drafts in the browser's own store and hands work to the existing hold operation; it adds no native operation and no second host
  forbidden_inference an offer observed on a page -> a verified price, stock, or a checkout quote
  forbidden_inference the live witness -> the extension working in the reader's own Chrome; branded Chrome refuses an unpacked extension from the command line, so it ran in Chrome for Testing 131 with a throwaway profile
  forbidden_inference confirmed: true in an envelope -> a person having asked; the host trusts the one extension its manifest names, and that extension sets it from a click
  known_gap install.sh, which registers the host in the reader's own browser, has not been run: it writes into that browser's configuration. The panel's "hold what I selected" button first asks the reader to grant the site, and no automation can answer that prompt, so that one path is exercised only through the port beneath it. The side panel was driven as a page in a tab, not docked beside one. The same limit holds for "compare or design from this page": the extension reads a tab only after the reader's click grants it, so the witness runs the extension's capture function in the page through the debugger instead.
  invariant scripts/recurring-commerce is canonical; scripts/project-recurring-commerce-browser.mjs generates exact self-contained extension copies and the consumer tests reject drift
  known_gap held selections have native Desk review and an explicit wiki_page draft form; this is not automatic recipe admission, offer verification, provider booking or task completion
  known_gap observe and capture read the page as a stranger: a separate browser with no session opens the address, so a page behind a sign-in is kept as its sign-in wall, not as the reader saw it

