architecture page-capture
  canonical_name PageCapture
  family external
  domain External / A page as the several things it is
  layer external
  semantic_question What arrived, what did the page become after its scripts ran, where was everything placed, what does it tell assistive technology, and how did it look -- for one reading?
  purpose One reading of a page kept as five representations bound to one capture identity: the response as the network delivered it, the document after its scripts ran, the layout with every node's box, the accessibility tree, and a picture. A later reader uses the representation that answers its question without loading the page again, and without asking a model to rediscover structure from a picture.
  maturity measured
  node_types PageCaptureRecord
  node_types PageRepresentation
  interacts browser-host
  source_path integrations/browser/capture/page-capture.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/tests/page-capture.test.mjs
  witness integrations/browser/tests/page-capture.test.mjs captures a page whose script adds a line after it arrives: the kept response is byte-for-byte what was served and lacks the line, the kept document has it, the accessibility tree names the button by its label and the heading by its text, the layout carries boxes and the added text, the picture is a PNG, every file matches the hash in the record, and a second reading of the same page has the same capture identity; an address that is not public https or carries credentials is refused
  internal_calculus Chrome runs headless in a throwaway profile with its sandbox on, on a debugging port it chooses and writes into that profile; the capture drives it over the DevTools protocol and removes the profile afterwards
  internal_calculus the identity is the address the page settled on, the response and the document. Layout, the accessibility tree and the picture carry session-local node numbers and pixels, so they are bound to the identity and do not define it
  invariant a representation is kept with its hash and size, and the record names what each one is
  invariant only a public https address is captured; one carrying credentials is refused
  forbidden_inference a captured page -> a true statement about what it describes
  forbidden_inference a label on the page (paid, in stock, approved) -> that state verified with whoever owns it
  forbidden_inference this capture -> what a signed-in reader sees; it was read as a stranger
  forbidden_inference a matching capture identity -> the page unchanged for another reader, viewport or moment
  known_gap nothing consumes a capture yet: ForeignTwin, DomainProfile and SubjectFabric read retained bodies, not these representations, and a capture is not recorded as a ForeignTwin observation with rights
  known_gap one viewport (1280x900), one bounded wait after load, no scrolling and no interaction; a page that loads content on scroll or after a click is captured as it first stood
  witness 2026-10-03 https://example.com/ captured twice for real, once directly (status 200, 38 accessibility nodes, five representations) and once from the extension's panel through the host
  known_gap public-page capture has been run on one simple page; nothing with a consent wall, heavy scripting or scrolled content

